{"step_index":13,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T16:43:32Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-23T22:13:32+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-23T22:13:32+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/Downloads/find-skill-repo/all%20github%20repos/OpenReels/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 266\nTotal Bytes: 12439\nShowing lines 1 to 266\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # OpenReels\r\n2: \r\n3: [![GitHub stars](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/tsensei/OpenReels?style=flat&color=f5c542)](https://github.com/tsensei/OpenReels/stargazers)\r\n4: [![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-blue.svg)](LICENSE)\r\n5: [![Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/version-0.13.1-green.svg)](CHANGELOG.md)\r\n6: [![Tests](https://img.shields.io/badge/tests-288%20passing-brightgreen.svg)]()\r\n7: [![TypeScript](https://img.shields.io/badge/TypeScript-5.x-3178c6.svg)]()\r\n8: [![Docker](https://img.shields.io/badge/Docker-ready-2496ED.svg)]()\r\n9: \r\n10: Open-source AI pipeline that turns any topic into a publish-ready YouTube/Instagram/TikTok Short. One command. Research, script, voiceover, AI-generated visuals, AI-generated music, animated captions, scene transitions. Out comes a vertical MP4, ready to upload.\r\n11: \r\n12: Web UI with live pipeline visualization, REST API, Docker, and CLI. Bring your own API keys.\r\n13: \r\n14: ## Demo\r\n15: \r\n16: <div align=\"center\">\r\n17: \r\n18: \r\n19: https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4df8893-7764-43c3-b004-ef610fec710f\r\n20: \r\n21: \r\n22: **Topic in, MP4 out.** This video was generated in a single command:\r\n23: \r\n24: ```bash\r\n25: openreels \"the apollo 13 disaster, from explosion to miraculous return\" --provider google\r\n26: ```\r\n27: \r\n28: </div>\r\n29: \r\n30: ### Web UI\r\n31: \r\n32: <div align=\"center\">\r\n33: <img src=\".github/assets/demo.gif\" alt=\"OpenReels Web UI demo\" width=\"800\" />\r\n34: \r\n35: **Live pipeline visualization.** Watch research, script, voiceover, visuals, music, and assembly stages stream in real time.\r\n36: </div>\r\n37: \r\n38: <details>\r\n39: <summary><strong>Screenshots</strong></summary>\r\n40: \r\n41: <table>\r\n42: <tr>\r\n43: <td><img src=\".github/assets/home.png\" alt=\"Home page\" width=\"400\" /></td>\r\n44: <td><img src=\".github/assets/pipeline.png\" alt=\"Pipeline running\" width=\"400\" /></td>\r\n45: </tr>\r\n46: <tr>\r\n47: <td align=\"center\"><em>Topic input with archetype gallery</em></td>\r\n48: <td align=\"center\"><em>Live pipeline with storyboard</em></td>\r\n49: </tr>\r\n50: <tr>\r\n51: <td><img src=\".github/assets/pipeline_completed.png\" alt=\"Pipeline completed\" width=\"400\" /></td>\r\n52: <td><img src=\".github/assets/gallery.png\" alt=\"Gallery view\" width=\"400\" /></td>\r\n53: </tr>\r\n54: <tr>\r\n55: <td align=\"center\"><em>Completed: video player, cost breakdown, quality review</em></td>\r\n56: <td align=\"center\"><em>Gallery with multiple generations</em></td>\r\n57: </tr>\r\n58: </table>\r\n59: \r\n60: </details>\r\n61: \r\n62: ## How it works\r\n63: \r\n64: Give it a topic. It handles everything:\r\n65: \r\n66: | Stage | What happens |\r\n67: |-------|-------------|\r\n68: | **Research** | Web search grounds the script in real facts, not hallucinations |\r\n69: | **Script** | Writes a punchy short-form script with scene breakdowns, visual direction, and emotional arc |\r\n70: | **Voiceover** | Generates TTS audio with word-level timestamps for karaoke-style captions |\r\n71: | **Visuals** | AI images (Gemini, DALL-E), AI video clips (Google Veo 3.1, fal.ai Kling 2.6 Pro) with dedicated cinematography prompts and negative prompt guidance, plus vision-verified stock footage that rejects bad matches and retries automatically |\r\n72: | **Music** | AI-generated background score via Google Lyria 3 Pro, scene-synced to match the video's emotional arc. Or pick from 25 bundled royalty-free tracks |\r\n73: | **Captions** | Spring-animated 3-state captions with 7 distinct styles, per-archetype theming, and word-level karaoke highlighting |\r\n74: | **Assembly** | Composites everything into a vertical MP4 via Remotion with crossfade, slide, wipe, and flip transitions |\r\n75: | **Critique** | AI critic scores the output. If quality is below threshold, the pipeline re-runs |\r\n76: \r\n77: Every stage streams live progress to the web UI. You watch the AI research, write, paint, compose, and render in real time.\r\n78: \r\n79: ## Provider flexibility\r\n80: \r\n81: Mix and match providers or go all-in on one ecosystem:\r\n82: \r\n83: | Capability | Providers |\r\n84: |-----------|-----------|\r\n85: | **LLM** | Anthropic Claude, OpenAI GPT, Google Gemini, OpenRouter (300+ models), any OpenAI-compatible endpoint |\r\n86: | **Search** | Native (provider built-in), Tavily, or parametric knowledge |\r\n87: | **TTS** | ElevenLabs, Inworld, OpenAI TTS, Gemini TTS, Kokoro (free, local) |\r\n88: | **Images** | Gemini Imagen, OpenAI DALL-E |\r\n89: | **Video** | Google Veo 3.1, fal.ai Kling 2.6 Pro (with cross-provider fallback, negative prompts, structured cinematography prompts) |\r\n90: | **Music** | Google Lyria 3 Pro (AI-generated, $0.08/track), Bundled library (free) |\r\n91: | **Stock** | Pexels, Pixabay (both searched, vision-verified, with AI fallback) |\r\n92: \r\n93: **One key, everything Google:** `--provider google` sets LLM, images, TTS, video, and music to Google APIs with a single `GOOGLE_API_KEY`.\r\n94: \r\n95: **Zero-cost voiceover:** `--provider local` uses Kokoro for free local TTS. No API key needed.\r\n96: \r\n97: ## Quickstart\r\n98: \r\n99: ### Web UI (recommended)\r\n100: \r\n101: ```bash\r\n102: git clone https://github.com/tsensei/OpenReels.git\r\n103: cd OpenReels\r\n104: cp .env.example .env   # fill in your API keys\r\n105: docker compose up      # starts Redis + API + Worker\r\n106: # Open http://localhost:3000\r\n107: ```\r\n108: \r\n109: Type a topic, pick your providers, and watch the pipeline run. Research, script, voiceover, visuals, music, and assembly stages stream live to the browser. Download the final video when it's done.\r\n110: \r\n111: ### Docker CLI (single run)\r\n112: \r\n113: ```bash\r\n114: cp .env.example .env   # fill in your API keys\r\n115: \r\n116: docker run --env-file .env --shm-size=2gb -v ./output:/output ghcr.io/tsensei/openreels \"5 stoic lessons that changed my life\"\r\n117: ```\r\n118: \r\n119: Or run through Docker Compose:\r\n120: \r\n121: ```bash\r\n122: docker compose run worker npx tsx src/index.ts --yes \"5 stoic lessons that changed my life\"\r\n123: ```\r\n124: \r\n125: ### Local development\r\n126: \r\n127: **Prerequisites:** Node.js 22+, pnpm, ffprobe\r\n128: \r\n129: ```bash\r\n130: git clone https://github.com/tsensei/OpenReels.git\r\n131: cd OpenReels\r\n132: pnpm install\r\n133: cp .env.example .env   # fill in your API keys\r\n134: ```\r\n135: \r\n136: ```bash\r\n137: # Full pipeline with AI music\r\n138: pnpm start \"the fall of the Roman Empire\" --provider google\r\n139: \r\n140: # Free local TTS, no API spend on voiceover\r\n141: pnpm start \"5 stoic lessons\" --provider local\r\n142: \r\n143: # Dry run (outputs DirectorScore JSON, no asset generation)\r\n144: pnpm start \"your topic\" --dry-run\r\n145: \r\n146: # Specific archetype and provider combo\r\n147: pnpm start \"your topic\" --archetype anime_illustration --provider openai\r\n148: \r\n149: # Creative direction file (guide the AI with a brief)\r\n150: pnpm start \"deep sea exploration\" --direction examples/direction-brief.md\r\n151: \r\n152: # Replay from a previous score (skip research + director, re-render)\r\n153: pnpm start \"your topic\" --score output/2026-04-10-111939-.../score.json\r\n154: ```\r\n155: \r\n156: ### API keys\r\n157: \r\n158: **Minimum to run** (pick one LLM + one TTS):\r\n159: - `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` or `OPENAI_API_KEY` or `GOOGLE_API_KEY` — [Anthropic](https://console.anthropic.com/) / [OpenAI](https://platform.openai.com/api-keys) / [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com/apikey)\r\n160: - `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` or `INWORLD_TTS_API_KEY` — [ElevenLabs](https://elevenlabs.io/) / [Inworld](https://inworld.ai/). Or use `--tts-provider kokoro` (free, no key), `--tts-provider openai-tts`, or `--tts-provider gemini-tts`\r\n161: - `GOOGLE_API_KEY` — also needed for Gemini image generation, AI video (Veo), AI music (Lyria), and Gemini TTS\r\n162: \r\n163: **Optional:** `PEXELS_API_KEY` ([Pexels](https://www.pexels.com/api/)), `PIXABAY_API_KEY` ([Pixabay](https://pixabay.com/api/docs/)) for stock footage, `FAL_API_KEY` ([fal.ai](https://fal.ai/)) for Kling video generation\r\n164: \r\n165: ### CLI flags\r\n166: \r\n167: | Flag | Description | Default |\r\n168: |------|-------------|---------|\r\n169: | `--provider <name>` | LLM provider (`anthropic`, `openai`, `gemini`, `openrouter`, `openai-compatible`, `google`, `local`) | `anthropic` |\r\n170: | `--llm-model <model>` | Model ID override (e.g. `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4` for OpenRouter) | provider default |\r\n171: | `--llm-base-url <url>` | Base URL for `openai-compatible` (e.g. `http://localhost:11434/v1`) | — |\r\n172: | `--search-provider <name>` | Search provider (`native`, `tavily`, `none`) | auto-detect |\r\n173: | `--image-provider <name>` | Image provider (`gemini`, `openai`) | `gemini` |\r\n174: | `--tts-provider <name>` | TTS provider (`elevenlabs`, `inworld`, `kokoro`, `gemini-tts`, `openai-tts`) | `elevenlabs` |\r\n175: | `--music-provider <name>` | Music provider (`bundled`, `lyria`) | `bundled` |\r\n176: | `--video-provider <name>` | Video provider (`gemini`, `fal`) | auto-detect |\r\n177: | `--archetype <name>` | Override visual archetype | LLM chooses |\r\n178: | `--platform <name>` | Target platform (`youtube`, `tiktok`, `instagram`) | `youtube` |\r\n179: | `--dry-run` | Output DirectorScore JSON without generating assets | off |\r\n180: | `--preview` | Open Remotion Studio after rendering | off |\r\n181: | `-o, --output <dir>` | Output directory | `./output` |\r\n182: | `--no-music` | Disable background music | music on |\r\n183: | `--no-video` | Disable AI video generation | video on |\r\n184: | `--no-stock-verify` | Disable VLM stock footage verification | verify on |\r\n185: | `--stock-confidence <n>` | Min confidence for stock verification (0-1) | `0.6` |\r\n186: | `--stock-max-attempts <n>` | Max stock API calls per scene | `4` |\r\n187: | `--video-model <model>` | Video model override | provider default |\r\n188: | `--kokoro-voice <voice>` | Kokoro voice preset | `af_heart` |\r\n189: | `--direction <file>` | Creative brief file (markdown) to guide the AI | — |\r\n190: | `--score <path>` | Replay from a saved `score.json`, skipping research + director | — |\r\n191: | `-y, --yes` | Auto-confirm cost estimation (Docker/CI) | off |\r\n192: \r\n193: ## Cost transparency\r\n194: \r\n195: Before spending any money, the pipeline shows a detailed cost breakdown and asks for confirmation:\r\n196: \r\n197: ```\r\n198: Estimated cost: $0.686\r\n199:   LLM:    $0.0029 (7 calls)\r\n200:   TTS:    $0.0171 (853 chars)\r\n201:   Images: $0.3030 (3 AI images @ $0.101/ea)\r\n202:   Video:  $0.3000 (1 AI videos)\r\n203:   Music:  $0.0802 (Lyria AI generation)\r\n204:   Stock:  free\r\n205: ```\r\n206: \r\n207: After rendering, actual cost is computed from real token usage. Use `--dry-run` to preview the DirectorScore without spending anything.\r\n208: \r\n209: ## Archetypes\r\n210: \r\n211: 14 visual styles that control colors, captions, motion, lighting, and AI image prompting. Same topic, four different archetypes:\r\n212: \r\n213: <div align=\"center\">\r\n214: <table>\r\n215: <tr>\r\n216: <td><img src=\".github/assets/kaldi_cinematic.jpg\" alt=\"Cinematic Documentary\" width=\"180\" /></td>\r\n217: <td><img src=\".github/assets/kaldi_anime.jpg\" alt=\"Anime Illustration\" width=\"180\" /></td>\r\n218: <td><img src=\".github/assets/kaldi_surreal.jpg\" alt=\"Surreal Dreamscape\" width=\"180\" /></td>\r\n219: <td><img src=\".github/assets/kaldi_vintage.jpg\" alt=\"Vintage Snapshot\" width=\"180\" /></td>\r\n220: </tr>\r\n221: <tr>\r\n222: <td align=\"center\"><em>Cinematic Documentary</em></td>\r\n223: <td align=\"center\"><em>Anime Illustration</em></td>\r\n224: <td align=\"center\"><em>Surreal Dreamscape</em></td>\r\n225: <td align=\"center\"><em>Vintage Snapshot</em></td>\r\n226: </tr>\r\n227: </table>\r\n228: </div>\r\n229: \r\n230: | Archetype | Best for |\r\n231: |-----------|----------|\r\n232: | `editorial_caricature` | News commentary, satire, social issues |\r\n233: | `warm_narrative` | Storytelling, history, human interest |\r\n234: | `studio_realism` | Professional photography, editorial, luxury |\r\n235: | `infographic` | Data, facts, explainers, rapid-fire content |\r\n236: | `anime_illustration` | Dynamic, action-oriented, pop culture |\r\n237: | `pastoral_watercolor` | Nature, contemplative, hand-painted aesthetic |\r\n238: | `comic_book` | Action, adventure, energetic content |\r\n239: | `gothic_fantasy` | Dark themes, mythology, epic content |\r\n240: | `vintage_snapshot` | Nostalgic, intimate, personal stories |\r\n241: | `surreal_dreamscape` | Sci-fi, fantasy, mind-bending topics |\r\n242: | `warm_editorial` | Lifestyle, people stories, general purpose |\r\n243: | `cinematic_documentary` | Factual, historical, science |\r\n244: | `moody_cinematic` | Mystery, tension, crime, dark history |\r\n245: | `bold_illustration` | Educational, how-to, listicles |\r\n246: \r\n247: ## Background\r\n248: \r\n249: OpenReels is a full rewrite of [ReelMistri](https://github.com/tsensei/ReelMistri/), a CLI pipeline originally built for Bangla-language YouTube Shorts automation. ReelMistri proved the concept: one command, fully produced video, language-aware scripts, culturally coherent visuals, proper Bengali text rendering.\r\n250: \r\n251: The rewrite moves from Python to TypeScript for native [Remotion](https://www.remotion.dev/) integration. Cleaner video rendering, better developer experience, no Python-to-TypeScript bridge.\r\n252: \r\n253: ## Status\r\n254: \r\n255: v0.17.0 shipped. See [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) for full version history and [TODOS.md](TODOS.md) for known issues and roadmap.\r\n256: \r\n257: ## Star History\r\n258: \r\n259: If OpenReels is useful to you, consider giving it a star. It helps others discover the project.\r\n260: \r\n261: [![Star History Chart](https://api.star-history.com/svg?repos=tsensei/OpenReels&type=Date)](https://star-history.com/#tsensei/OpenReels&Date)\r\n262: \r\n263: ## License\r\n264: \r\n265: This project is licensed under the [MIT License](LICENSE).\r\n266: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
